    "- precautions of single and multi linear regression.\n",
    "\n",
    "___OVERFITTING:-\n",
    "\n",
    "- when model is overfittied means it is having graph, in which data point are in straight line form but the best fit line or here we will call it as overfitting line is connecting all the data points , which shows the model does not have any error , which makes it a bad model as it is 100% accurate.here error=0, and ut wont follow y=mx+c the straight line eq.\n",
    "\n",
    "- when we will get good accuracy for training data and bad accuracy for testing data, then it is overfitting. \n",
    "\n",
    "- when error is near 0 or equal to 0.\n",
    "\n",
    "-in overfitting the bias is low and variance is high.\n",
    "\n",
    "- it mostly happens with regression data .\n",
    "\n",
    "- Bias: when data is biased in nature it means, the error is present and it will always low.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Variance: when the accuracy of the training and test data changes in large numbers  everytime the data is shuffling . when the accuracy come the different everytime we say the data has high variance,\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "4628b910-d997-446e-816c-8ca68b70114f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "___UNDERFITTING:-\n",
    "\n",
    "- it happens with classification data.\n",
    "\n",
    "- in graph , when there are classes present , the line will seperate the classes .\n",
    "\n",
    "- bias: here it will be high , which means the error rate will be very much high.\n",
    "\n",
    "- variance: here it will be very low, which means after the shuffling the accuracy wont change.\n",
    "\n",
    "- it is good for test data and poor for trainig data.\n",
    "\n",
    "-here all the predictions will be worng as the model is not getting enough training data to learn features."
   ]
  },
  {
